  "title": "Octave numbers",
  "summary": "A number after the letter says exactly which key you mean. Middle C is C4.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Octave number",
      "body": "To say exactly which C you mean, add a number. Middle C is **C4**. The C an octave above is C5, and the C an octave below is C3. This number is the **octave number**. It goes up by one at every C, so the B just below middle C is B3.\n\n**Why it matters:** \"Play an E\" could mean any of seven Es. \"Play E4\" means exactly one key, so octave numbers let the app, a teacher or a score point to one exact key.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        59,
        60,
        62
      ],
      "labels": {
        "59": "B3",
        "60": "C4",
        "62": "D4"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "show",
      "title": "C3, C4 and C5",
      "body": "Three Cs, an octave apart. The middle one is middle C, C4.",
      "highlightMidi": [
        48,
        60,
        72
      ],
      "labels": {
        "48": "C3",
        "60": "C4",
        "72": "C5"
